IN THE SUPREME COURT OF INDIA
CASE NO: Civil Appeal No. 2568 of 2020
CITATION: (2020) 7 SCC 469
YEAR: 2020

CORAM / BENCH:
Hon'ble Judges: D.Y. Chandrachud, Ajay Rastogi

PARTIES:
Secretary MoD vs Babita Puniya & Ors

STATUTES & ACTS REFERRED:
Constitution of India, Army Act, 1950

KEY PROVISIONS & SECTIONS:
Article 14, Article 16, Article 15

LEGAL KEYWORDS & TOPICS:
permanent commission for women, gender stereotypes rejected, command appointments in army

================================================================================
                    JUDGMENT SUMMARY & RATIO DECIDENDI
================================================================================

Landmark verdict directing the grant of Permanent Commission to Women Short Service Commission Officers in the Indian Army, striking down institutional gender barriers.

1. ISSUES CONSIDERED:
   The court addressed questions of legal interpretation under Article 14, Article 16, Article 15.

2. ANALYSIS & PRECEDENT CONTEXT:
   Having examined the statutory scheme, fundamental principles of jurisprudence,
   and constitutional safeguards, the Court reiterated the necessity of strict
   compliance with statutory procedure and evidentiary standards.

3. HELD & BINDING RATIO:
   The principle formulated in this judgment constitutes binding judicial precedent
   within its territorial and appellate jurisdiction.

